From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] bfd: aarch64 PE: resolve weak externals before applying
 relocations

GCC emits a PE weak external (C_NT_WEAK, with an aux record naming the
default definition, ".weak.<name>.<other>") for a function declared
__attribute__((weak)).  bfd keeps such a symbol undefined (undefweak) in
the hash table, so coff_pe_aarch64_relocate_section found no definition,
skipped the relocation and left it to _bfd_coff_generic_relocate_section.
That one does resolve the weak external, but cannot apply the AArch64
relocations: it prints "26 bit relocation not currently supported." and
writes the default definition's offset in its section as the branch
displacement.  The call lands in some other function.

gnutls's library constructor calls its weak _gnutls_global_init_skip()
that way and jumped into the middle of _gnutls_memory_mark_undefined();
the unbalanced stack made every program linked with msys-gnutls-30.dll
crash while the DLL was loading.  util-linux's libcommon has the same
pattern (blkdev.c, timeutils.c, randutils.c).

Resolve the weak external to its default definition, as the generic code
does, before the AArch64 relocations are applied.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
--- a/bfd/coff-aarch64.c
+++ b/bfd/coff-aarch64.c
@@ -565,6 +565,27 @@
 	    }
 	  }
 
+      /* A PE weak external (C_NT_WEAK with an aux record, which is what
+	 GCC emits for __attribute__((weak)) definitions) stays undefined in
+	 the hash table; its default definition is the symbol the aux record
+	 names.  Resolve it here, as _bfd_coff_generic_relocate_section
+	 does: the generic code cannot apply the AArch64 relocations below
+	 and would, for instance, write the target's section offset into a
+	 BRANCH26 as the branch displacement.  */
+      if (h
+	  && (h->root.type == bfd_link_hash_undefweak
+	      || h->root.type == bfd_link_hash_undefined)
+	  && h->symbol_class == C_NT_WEAK && h->numaux == 1)
+	{
+	  struct coff_link_hash_entry *h2 = NULL;
+	  unsigned long symndx2 = h->aux->x_sym.x_tagndx.u32;
+
+	  if (symndx2 < obj_raw_syment_count (h->auxbfd))
+	    h2 = obj_coff_sym_hashes (h->auxbfd)[symndx2];
+	  if (h2 && h2->root.type == bfd_link_hash_defined)
+	    h = h2;
+	}
+
       if (h && h->root.type == bfd_link_hash_defined)
 	{
 	  sec = h->root.u.def.section;
-- 
